  "description": "Mermaid diagrams drawn by Pele (Obsidian 1.15 and later; research/14 section 6.196). Same method as mermaid.json: every block of `note` is drawn twice in the isolated Obsidian -- as Obsidian draws it with the theme applied, and as a REFERENCE, the same text drawn by the same Pele in a host that is not under the theme, styled by Inkdrop's own Mermaid-plugin stylesheet (tests/fixtures/inkdrop-pele-mermaid.css, from Inkdrop 6.3.0's `mermaid` package, MIT) with its --mermaid-* tokens resolved from the palette -- and the painted properties of the two are compared element by element. The light scheme compares Obsidian's own colours (theme not applied) with a plain Pele host. The 32 diagram types Pele 1.8.0 draws are all covered; Pele puts no inline !important on colours, so there is no inlineImportant.",
